  body: "# DMG outcome decision\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nAn outcome decision communicates the result of
    a claim or application and incorporates subsidiary determinations, including entitlement elements and the day
    payment begins.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe distinction between the outcome and its component findings
    matters for challenges. Annex D and Annex E determine the appealable and non-appealable categories; these two
    paragraphs do not enumerate them.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 01101, PDF page 17](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68e8e657cf65bd04bad76752/dmg-v-1-ch-01.pdf#page=17)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 1: Principles of decision making and evidence.\n- [DMG 01102, PDF page 17](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68e8e657cf65bd04bad76752/dmg-v-1-ch-01.pdf#page=17)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 1: Principles of decision making and evidence.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch1` PDF SHA-256: `58b168c7b0a01f54713f6cfa60953549ebc099cbe568ffaeea551d0b756495d2`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `cf7a000e2c54c5361a03ec4ad73fa22cc14e8cdb0d4f03b53919a4a509a6eacb`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-prescribed-claim
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: An outcome decision is described as the decision on a claim or application; this does not mean
      that every application is a claim.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch1/0017
      quote: "01101 The decision on a claim or application is called an outcome decision because it tells the claimant\n\
        the outcome of the claim or application. An outcome decision incorporates all subsidiary determinations\n\
        such as the separate elements of entitlement to benefit and the day that benefit will be paid."
      locator: DMG 01101
  - target: term/dmg-first-tier-appeal
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The paragraph links appeal rights to outcome decisions while distinguishing subsidiary findings
      and referring to the annexes.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch1/0017
      quote: "01102 The claimant has a right of appeal against outcome decisions only 1 as listed in Annex D to
        this\nVolume. An outcome decision on a claim, for example, is whether or not the claimant is entitled to\n\
        benefit. As part of the process of making that decision, the DM makes determinations or findings of fact\n\
        which lead to the outcome. These determinations generally do not have the right of appeal - see Annex\n\n\
        E2. Although an appeal is against the outcome decision, in practice the claimant may wish to focus on a\n\
        component part of the decision. For further details on appeals see DMG Chapter 06."
      locator: DMG 01102
